│   │   └── services/           20 services métier
│   ├── tests/                  16 fichiers pytest
│   └── requirements.txt
├── frontend/              React 18 + Vite + PWA
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── pages/              51 pages JSX
│   │   │   ├── superadmin/     9 pages admin (Dashboard, Tenants, Users, Plans, Flags, Models, Audit, Broadcast, System, 2FA)
│   │   │   └── worker/         6 pages PWA
│   │   ├── components/         composants réutilisables
│   │   ├── layouts/            MainLayout, WorkerLayout, SuperAdminLayout
│   │   ├── services/api.js     tous les appels API
│   │   ├── context/            AuthContext, ThemeContext, SidebarContext
│   │   └── hooks/              useWebSocket, usePWAVersion, useNetworkSync
│   └── tests/e2e/             Playwright tests
├── ai_assets/             modèles YOLO (.pt files)
│   ├── animal_weights/    bee, goat, cow, chicken, rabbit, cow_behavior
│   └── plantations/       olive, insects, lemon, orange, leaves, plantdoc
├── monitoring/            Prometheus + Grafana + Mosquitto
├── workers/               workers IA (CV, anomalie, recommandation)
├── iot/                   ESP32 nodes (PlatformIO + Wokwi)
├── mlruns.db              MLflow registry (19 modèles enregistrés)
├── docker-compose.yml     prod: PostgreSQL + Redis + Mosquitto + backend + frontend
└── .github/workflows/     ci.yml (5 jobs) + cd.yml (Docker push + SSH deploy)
```

## MODÈLES DE BASE DE DONNÉES (domain.py)
Tables importantes :
- `users` — id, username, email, role, plan, plan_expires_at, stripe_customer_id, totp_secret, totp_enabled
- `farms` — id, owner_id (FK users), name, latitude, longitude, status
- `animal_units` — id, farm_id (FK farms), name, animal_type_id
- `sensors` — id, unit_id, sensor_type, sensor_id, is_active, last_seen, metadata (JSON)
- `telemetry_records` — IoT sensor readings
- `alerts` — id, unit_id, alert_type, message, severity, is_resolved
- `recommendations` — id, unit_id, probable_cause, recommendation_text, urgency_level, confidence_score, is_actioned
- `audit_logs` — id, admin_id, action, target_id, detail, ip_address
- `broadcasts` — id, title, body, target (all|owner|worker)
- `push_tokens` — id, user_id, token, platform
- `bee_hives`, `bee_visits`, `bee_productions`, `bee_expenses`, `bee_stock` — module apiculture
- `poultry_batches`, `poultry_feed_logs`, `poultry_health_logs`, `poultry_egg_logs` — module volaille

## SÉCURITÉ
- JWT HS256 (7 jours) + refresh token (30 jours)
- `require_superadmin` → dependency FastAPI pour routes superadmin
- `require_roles("owner", "superadmin")` → multi-role
- `FarmGuard` → isolation multi-tenant (farm_id scoping)
- Rate limiting via SlowAPI
- 2FA TOTP (pyotp) disponible pour superadmin

## PLANS D'ABONNEMENT
- `free`       → max 50 animaux, 1 worker, 1 ferme
- `pro`        → illimité animaux, 5 workers, 3 fermes — 29€/mois (Stripe)
- `enterprise` → tout illimité — sur mesure

## PATTERNS BACKEND À RESPECTER

### Endpoint standard
```python
from fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, HTTPException, Query
from app.core.security import get_current_user, require_roles
from app.core.farm_guard import get_scoped_farm_ids
from app.core.database import get_db
from app.core.cache import cached, cache_delete

router = APIRouter(prefix="/ma-ressource", tags=["Ma Ressource"])

@router.get("")
@cached("ma_ressource", ttl=300)  # Redis cache 5min
def list_items(
    farm_ids: list[int] = Depends(get_scoped_farm_ids),  # isolation multi-tenant
    db: Session = Depends(get_db),
    user = Depends(get_current_user),
):
    ...

@router.post("", status_code=201)
def create_item(data: MySchema, db=Depends(get_db), user=Depends(require_roles("owner"))):
    cache_delete("ma_ressource:*")  # invalider le cache
    ...
```

### Sérialisation standard
```python
def _serialize_item(obj) -> dict:
    return {
        "id": obj.id,
        "created_at": obj.created_at.isoformat() if obj.created_at else None,
        # ... tous les champs nécessaires
    }
```

### Ne jamais :
- Exposer `password_hash` dans les réponses
- Utiliser `farm_id = 1` hardcodé — toujours venir de FarmGuard ou du token
- Skiper `get_scoped_farm_ids` pour les endpoints de listing
- Créer des migrations sans ALTER TABLE idempotent (SQLite compatible)

## PATTERNS FRONTEND À RESPECTER

### Appel API
```javascript
// Toujours utiliser les fonctions de src/services/api.js
import { recsAPI, alertsAPI, farmsAPI } from '../services/api';

// Pattern standard dans un composant
const [data, setData] = useState([]);
const load = async () => {
  try {
    const { data: d } = await recsAPI.list(false, farmId);
    setData(d);
  } catch (e) { toast.error('Erreur chargement'); }
};
useEffect(() => { load(); }, [farmId]);
```

### Auth context
```javascript
const { user, farmId, farms, logout } = useAuth();
// user.role === 'superadmin' | 'owner' | 'worker'
// farmId → ferme sélectionnée active
```

### Design tokens (DARK THEME)
```javascript
const T = {
  bg: '#0a0e14', card: '#0d1520', border: '#1a2535',
  muted: '#4b6380', text: '#e2e8f0', text2: '#94a3b8',
  green: '#22c55e', red: '#ef4444', amber: '#f59e0b',
  blue: '#06b6d4', purple: '#7c3aed',
};
```

### Ne jamais :
- Utiliser `localStorage.getItem('token')` directement → utiliser `useAuth()`
- Coder un farm_id en dur → toujours depuis `useAuth().farmId`
- Créer des styles CSS globaux → inline styles ou classes existantes
- Importer depuis `'../../../'` → utiliser des imports courts

